:02:13.304230+00:00", "2026-09-17T22:45:45.509428+00:00", "2026-09-18T00:22:28.684959+00:00", "2026-09-18T00:23:01.135649+00:00", "2026-09-18T00:23:01.201620+00:00", "2026-09-18T00:50:37.882527+00:00", "2026-09-18T00:54:49.323640+00:00", "2026-09-18T00:55:40.445730+00:00"], "gates": {"python3 ci/scripts/check_constitution_anchors.py": {"rc": 0}, "python3 ci/scripts/check_constitution_anchors.py  # measured ~0.04s": {"rc": 0}, "python3 ci/scripts/check_doc_parity.py": {"rc": 0}, "python3 ci/scripts/check_doc_parity.py  # measured ~0.04s": {"rc": 0}, "python3 ci/scripts/check_no_consumer_names.py": {"rc": 0}, "python3 ci/scripts/check_no_consumer_names.py  # measured ~1.81s": {"rc": 0}, "python3 ci/scripts/check_swarm_bijection.py": {"rc": 0}, "python3 ci/scripts/check_swarm_bijection.py  # measured ~0.07s": {"rc": 0}}, "head_sha": "5a06604125338f5d302bf14fe82ab9c95eb40e1a", "pre_fix_sha": "5a06604125338f5d302bf14fe82ab9c95eb40e1a", "residual_risk": "Every attack here was executed on the consolidated tip (the post-fix tree), not on each block's own pre-fix sha: every audit blocked on the tip it read and the fixes landed as the next commits, so the pre-fix witnesses are the audits' own executed evidence and the relay artifacts per block. The identity unit's cache-reuse admission and definition-hash fold are EXCISED by the contract's pre-committed stop rule (the same-crate ProbedOp construction oracle could not be made complete: a use-rename and a mutated-copy return stayed invisible); the typed PROBED_OPS table stays with cross-crate sealing proven by the compiler and NO same-crate property claimed, because nothing folds an admission row into a durable hash. #546 and #562 item 3 stay open with the blind spots recorded. The two syn call-site oracles (submit seam, raw deleters) record the target path in any expression position over every compiled non-test .rs file; their residual is a bypass that duplicates the seam's body, caught by the oracle and never by the type system. The placed-gang birth epoch is read before probe_claim and begin_release's flip-before-bump order is pinned by a park point; the claim loop's own epoch path is unchanged. GRAPH (#515) is excised by its pre-committed stop rule and stays open with four executed design rounds. The #551 mining byte pin is captured from this PR's first Linux CI run and committed as a follow-up on the same PR. The lead-gate library's own residual arms, each marked `# R12-RESIDUAL` and each a rejection or a bounded run rather than a proof \u2014 _pre_fix_anticipation_rejection, _r12_anticipation_rejection, _r12_attack_command_denied, _r12_is_inspector_only, _r12_mutations_array_rejection, _r12_validate_and_run_entry, _resolve_worktree_cwd, _run_attack_command, cmd_export_anticipation, cmd_export_attestation \u2014 stay residuals: an attack command is re-executed and hash-matched at check time in a clean worktree, never re-derived; an inspector-only command proves presence, not behaviour; the mutations array is a labeled sample capped at three, never an exhaustive sweep.", "ts": "2026-09-18T03:50:41.150607+00:00", "unit_branch": "feat/500-wave6"}
